s://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000009/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"","translation":"","language":"Japanese"},{"page":50,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000010/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"遠志\nすずめはぎ 江戸\n\n山野陽地ニあり小草\n苗ハ絡石ニ似タリ\n春月葉ノ間ヨリ小紫花ヲ\n開ク後扁莢ヲ結ブ根ハ\n白色ナリ\n\n細葉ノ物\n上品ナリ\n\n長葉のかきのした\n\n本草圖譜 巻之八\n\n[illegible]","translation":"Polygala (tōshi / \"distant ambition\")\nKnown as suzume-hagi (sparrow bush-clover), Edo\n\nA small herb found in sunny spots in mountains and fields.\nIts seedlings resemble climbing fig (rakuseki).\nIn spring, small purple flowers emerge from between the leaves;\nafter they open, flat pods form. The root is\nwhite in color.\n\nThe fine-leaved variety\nis considered the superior grade.\n\nLong-leaved kakinoshita (a related plant with long leaves)\n\nIllustrated Materia Medica (Honzō Zufu), Volume 8\n\n[illegible]","language":"Japanese"},{"page":51,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000011/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"","translation":"","language":"Japanese"},{"page":52,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000012/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"","translation":"","language":"Japanese"},{"page":53,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000013/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"","translation":"","language":"Japanese"},{"page":54,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000014/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg","text":"","translation":"","language":"Japanese"},{"page":55,"image":"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gdc:gdcwdl:wd:l_:11:83:6_:00:1:wdl_11836_001:1287115_R0000015/full/pc